# Django App Structure (Preferred)

## Target layout (new work)

```text
your_app/
├── models.py
├── admin.py
├── filters.py
├── api/
│   ├── urls.py
│   ├── views.py
│   ├── serializers.py
│   └── openapi.py
├── services/
├── utils/
├── management/
├── tests/
└── docs/
    ├── frontend/
    └── backend/
```

- Group features inside shared files with section headers (`# === ... ===`).
- Put workflows in `services/`; reusable helpers in `utils/`.
- Do not invent a nested `api/v1/<app_name>/` package as the app-local layout.

## Legacy compatibility (important)

Existing feature-suffixed modules are **valid until a dedicated refactor**, for example:

- `maintenance/api/pm_views.py`
- `maintenance/api/transfer_views.py`
- parallel `*_serializers.py` / schema modules

When editing those files:

1. Do **not** treat their existence as a violation requiring an immediate merge/rename.
2. Prefer adding **new** endpoints to consolidated `views.py` / `serializers.py` / `openapi.py` when practical.
3. If you touch a legacy feature heavily, migrate that feature incrementally only when safe (imports, URLs, tests).

